n cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 1.1% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 9% and FFO growth of 4.7% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.4x depreciation (8.1% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (1.0%), and institutions hold 94%.","It returns 4.6% a year to shareholders (0.0% in buybacks and 4.8% in dividends).","The share count has grown 15.7% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It pays out 232% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["With about 285 employees, each generates about $1.7M of revenue, 0.7x the Real Estate median, and productivity has fallen 6.4% a year.","CEO pay is $2.4M (1x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $39K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":29,"head":"Avoid: the model rates it PASS.","pros":["Returns 4.6% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Model rating PASS (composite 21, gates 5/26)","ROIC 6.5% vs WACC 7.9%","Revenue shrank 10.8%/yr over 5y","P/E 34.8x vs sector 23.6x"],"flags":["The model rates it PASS"],"need":[],"buy_below":18.68,"vc":{"base":21.98,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":21.98,"n_alt":3,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.8396,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (84% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":23.5593,"ev_ebitda":16.316,"pfcf":17.832,"pb":1.3568,"roic":0.0411,"gross_margin":0.5765,"fcf_margin":0.1733,"div_yield":0.0479}},"ticker":"RYN","date":"2026-11-06"}